<file path="CONVENTIONS.md">
# Conventions

- ES modules, Node 20 or newer, no dependencies.
- One module per file in `src/`, named exports only, a JSDoc comment on every exported function.
- Tests live in `test/<module>.test.js` and use `node:test` with `node:assert/strict`.
- Run the whole suite with `npm test` (it runs `node --test`).
- Two-space indentation, single quotes, semicolons.
</file>

<file path="README.md">
# invoicekit

Invoicing helpers for Studio Lumen, a small design studio. Plain Node.js (ES modules), no dependencies.

- `src/catalogue.js`: the product catalogue (`data/catalogue.json`)
- `src/customers.js`: customers (`data/customers.json`)
- `src/money.js`: money helpers
- `src/result.js`, `src/errors.js`: results and error codes

Run the tests with `npm test`.
</file>

